# ── git here is for the CODE, and only the code. ───────────────────────────
# The art, models, sounds and .vox libraries are hundreds of megabytes, binary,
# and effectively static. They are irreplaceable, but they do not need per-line
# history and putting them in git makes every command crawl. Back them up
# separately (a drive or a cloud folder). Git is for the thing that CHANGES.

# whole trees of assets
art/
.vox/
sound/
website/assets/
website/sound/
website/old/
website/_snapshots/

# and a belt-and-braces rule by extension, so nothing binary can creep back in
*.vox
*.wav
*.mp3
*.obj
*.png
*.jpg
*.ico
*.otf
*.ttf
*.bak
*.log
node_modules/
